<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 0.862 mln bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 0.862 mln bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's cotton output reached 0.862 million 375-lb bales during the 1996/97 (July-June) crop year, Pakistan Cotton Ginners Association said Sunday.</p>
<p>Aijazuddin Ghauri, secretary of the association, said cotton arrival in the period ended September rose to 0.862 million bales in the 1996/97 crop year, compared to the 1995/96 production figure of 0.549 million.</p>
<p>Ghauri said textile mills had purchased 0.682 million bales and the balance was in the ginneries.</p>
<p>Brokers say cotton output was likely to surpass 1995/96 production figure of 9.95 million bales.</p>
<p>--Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
